### Charts
Build Vega-Lite specs with `chart.spec(mark, data=..., encoding=...)`, `chart.field(name, type, ...)` for channels, and `chart.layer`/`hconcat`/`vconcat` to combine specs; attach the result with `io.display(spec, title?)`. Charts show the shape of your data — use `stats` for the numbers. When the `charts` extension is granted, `ext.charts.line(...)`, `area`, `bar`, `scatter`, `histogram` and `heatmap` build ready-made specs. Over MCP each display returns a one-line summary; pass `images=true` to `exec`, `run_sections` (single section) or `read_section` to also get a PNG snapshot when you need a visual check (requires a server-side renderer; otherwise the summary says the image is unavailable).

### Notebook tools
- `{{.Prefix}}notebook()` — the outline: every section's state (`not_run`/`fresh`/`stale`/`failed`), `defines`/`reads name ← provider`, observed effects, `blocked:` diagnostics, and next-step guidance. Read it before running or editing code you did not write this session.
- `{{.Prefix}}exec(code, section={name, description?, rerun?, after?})` — saves/replaces the named section with this code BEFORE running it; failed code is preserved as a failed section. Always pass `section`: every execution belongs to a section so its inputs and outputs stay visible. Running it first runs every upstream section that is not fresh, in dependency order — the response's `upstream` lists what ran or was reused.
- `{{.Prefix}}run_sections(sections, dry_run?)` — run `"all"`, `"stale"`, one name, or a list of names, in dependency order (each section's non-fresh upstream runs first). `dry_run: true` previews the plan — `planned`/`reused`/`skipped` per section — without executing. Stops at the first failure; bulk runs skip `once` sections that already succeeded unless needed upstream. If the runtime is lost mid-run the report comes back with `restored: true` — earlier sections executed in the previous runtime, the rest are `not_run`, and the process is now EMPTY: do not blindly retry side effects.
- `{{.Prefix}}read_section(name)` — one section's code + metadata (`include_output` adds the last run's output/error).
- `{{.Prefix}}add_section(name, code, description?, rerun?, after_section?)` — write a section WITHOUT running it.

### Notebook rules
- There are no scratch execs: every exec belongs to a named section, so what a section reads and defines stays visible in the notebook.
- A section's state is derived over the graph: `fresh` ran ok on current code with fresh inputs; `stale` its code changed or a section it reads is not fresh; `failed` its current code errored; `not_run` never ran this incarnation.
- Editing a section makes it stale, and staleness propagates to every section that reads its defines. `rerun: "once"` marks sections bulk runs should skip after one success.
- Fix `blocked:` diagnostics before running the affected sections — an ambiguous name, a missing provider, or a cycle refuses the run with `graph_blocked`. Unrelated broken sections do not block.
- If the instance was restored after a loss, memory and files are EMPTY and nothing re-ran: your first exec/run returns `instance_restored` WITHOUT executing. Afterwards, run the sections you need — do not assume anything from before the loss exists.

